2026-09-25T00:28:52.4280989Z [36;1m# "unformatted" verdict, the only one this gate exists to produce.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4281804Z [36;1m# `rc=$?` never ran, the `GITHUB_OUTPUT` write never ran,[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4282626Z [36;1m# `continue-on-error` swallowed the death, and the scope step below[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4283524Z [36;1m# fell back to `${GUARD_RC:-2}`. 2 is a REFUSAL, so it printed NO[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4284315Z [36;1m# VERDICT and scored neutral, and the job concluded success.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4284944Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4285476Z [36;1m# THE GUARD THREW ITS ANSWER AWAY ONLY WHEN IT HAD ONE. A formatted[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4286337Z [36;1m# tree exits 0, `-e` does not fire, and rc=0 published normally — so[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4287196Z [36;1m# the failure was exclusive to the case the gate is for, which is why[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4287919Z [36;1m# it survived unnoticed.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4288359Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4289138Z [36;1m# `scripts/format-check.sh` has NO `exit 2` path (its codes are 0, 1,[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4289973Z [36;1m# 3, 4, 5, 6; the one `exit 2` in the file is inside a selftest[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4290738Z [36;1m# fixture), so "guard exit 2" could never have come from the guard.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4291509Z [36;1m# It was the `:-2` default on an unset variable.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4292047Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4292564Z [36;1m# Do NOT replace this with `set +e`: that is a mode change a later[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4293451Z [36;1m# edit can silently undo by re-adding strictness. `|| rc=$?` is local[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4294285Z [36;1m# to this one call and cannot be undone from a distance.[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4294885Z [36;1mrc=0[0m
2026-09-25T00:28:52.4295379Z [36;1mbash scripts/format-check.sh > "$log" 2>&1 || rc=$?[0m
